1
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,130
- Hey.     - Hey, ha, ha.

2
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:23,310
Monica?

3
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:25,980
What time is it?

4
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:28,230
Uh, 9.

5
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:31,400
But it's dark out.

6
00:00:31,570 --> 00:00:34,780
Um, well, that's because you always sleep till noon, silly.

7
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,740
This is what 9 looks like.

8
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:42,240
I guess I'll get washed up then.

9
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:44,870
Watch that sunrise.

10
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,170
I'm really getting tired of sneaking around all the time.

11
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:54,630
I know, me too. Hey, what if we went away for the whole weekend? No interruptions.

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,930
And we could be naked the entire time.

13
00:00:57,510 --> 00:00:58,550
All weekend?

14
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,430
- That's a whole lot of naked.     - Mm-hm.

15
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:05,060
Yeah, I could say I have a conference and you can say you have a chef thing.

16
00:01:05,230 --> 00:01:08,270
Oh, I've always wanted to go to this culinary fair in Jersey!

17
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:10,610
Ha, ha, okay. You know you're not, though.

18
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:12,940
- Right. Okay.     - Let's go.

19
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:15,650
Wait. What about Joey?

20
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,830
Hey, guess what I'm doing this weekend.

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,960
Going to this culinary fair in Jersey.

22
00:02:14,130 --> 00:02:18,880
How weird! Chandler just told us he's got a conference there. Huh.

23
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:23,350
Oh, that's funny, ha, ha. Seems like Chandler's conference could've been in Connecticut or Vermont.

24
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:31,270
I'm not in charge of where the conference is held.

25
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:35,320
Do you want people to think it's a fake conference? It's a real conference.

26
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,280
- Hey.JOEY     - Hey.

27
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:40,320
- Is Rachel here? I gotta talk to her.     - No, she's out shopping.

28
00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:43,570
- Damn.     - What's going on?

29
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,830
I told Emily to come.

30
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:50,000
And I just need to, you know, talk to Rachel about it.

31
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,000
Wait a minute.

32
00:02:53,170 --> 00:02:56,380
So when Emily comes, you're not gonna see Rachel anymore?

33
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:59,630
I'm focusing on the "I get to see my wife" part, all right...

34
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,340
...and not on the part that makes me do this, huh?

35
00:03:06,010 --> 00:03:09,890
So you'll never be in the same room together? How is that even gonna work?

36
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:12,560
I have no idea. I mean...

37
00:03:12,730 --> 00:03:15,730
But I assure you, I will figure it out.

38
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,360
It doesn't seem like it's gonna work.

39
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,490
- Hi, guys.     - Hi.

40
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:24,910
- Hey.     - Hey.

41
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,370
What's going on?

42
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:29,870
We're flipping Monica's mattress.

43
00:03:32,370 --> 00:03:36,540
So I'm thinking, basically, we pick it up, and then we flip it.

44
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:40,210
That's better than my way.

45
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:44,510
Oh, hey, guys, would you flip mine too?

46
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,850
Oh, man

47
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,180
Oh, look! A letter from my mom.

48
00:03:54,020 --> 00:03:56,610
So, Rach?

49
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:58,940
You know how Emily's coming, right?

50
00:03:59,150 --> 00:04:00,820
Oh, yeah. I know.

51
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,150
Can you hear anything?

52
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:05,030
Oh, yeah, somebody just said, "Can you hear anything?"

53
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:13,000
Hey, Joey's ass.

54
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:16,460
What are you doing?

55
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:19,420
Remember when they got in that big fight and broke up...

56
00:04:19,590 --> 00:04:22,420
...and we were all stuck in here all night with no food?

57
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:26,590
Well, when Ross said "Rachel" at the wedding, I figured it was gonna happen again.

58
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:28,640
You know? So I hid this in here.

59
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:31,930
Ooh, candy bars, crossword puzzles...

60
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:34,310
Ooh, Mad Libs. Mine!

61
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:37,350
Condoms?

62
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:43,030
Hey, you don't know how long we're gonna be in here.

63
00:04:43,190 --> 00:04:45,360
We may have to re-populate the Earth.

64
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:49,780
And condoms are the way to do that?

65
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:56,160
Anyway, it all boils down to this.

66
00:04:56,330 --> 00:05:00,920
- The last time I talked to Emily...     - Aah! Oh, my God! Our dog died!

67
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:06,840
- What?     - Oh, my God. LaPooh, our dog!

68
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:09,680
LaPooh's still alive?

69
00:05:09,890 --> 00:05:14,680
Oh! It says he was hit by an ice-cream truck and dragged for...

70
00:05:14,850 --> 00:05:18,690
...19 blocks!

71
00:05:19,110 --> 00:05:23,150
- Oh! Oh, my God.     - Sweetie, we heard you crying.

72
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:26,190
- Please don't cry.     - It's LaPooh!

73
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,740
I know, it's LaPooh right now but it'll get better.

74
00:05:36,460 --> 00:05:39,080
I can't believe it! We're here!

75
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,750
Ooh, chocolates on the pillows! Oh, I love that!

76
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,840
You should live with Joey. Rolos everywhere.

77
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:51,090
- Oh. Okay, I'll be right back.     - Okay.

78
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:57,100
Oh, yes!

79
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:00,560
Monica, get in here. It's a high-speed car chase on!

80
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:02,610
We're switching rooms.

81
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:04,780
Oh, dear God, they gave us glasses!

82
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,530
No, they gave us glasses with lipstick on them.

83
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:12,200
If they didn't change the glasses, who knows what else they didn't change.

84
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:16,540
Oh, come on, sweetie. I just want this weekend to be perfect, okay?

85
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:18,960
- We can change rooms, can't we?     - Okay.

86
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:23,420
Okay, but let's do it now, though, because Chopper 5 just lost its feed!

87
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:30,090
Hey, so, uh...

88
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:33,260
You know how there was something I wanted to talk to you about?

89
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:35,220
Oh, yeah.

90
00:06:35,390 --> 00:06:37,350
Well...

91
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,730
...you know I'm trying to work things out with Emily.

92
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,770
Mm-hm.

93
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:43,690
Well, there's this...

94
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,820
...one thing.

95
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:49,610
Okay, here goes.

96
00:06:53,490 --> 00:06:55,740
I made a promise that... Oh, hey.

97
00:06:55,910 --> 00:06:57,950
- What?     - Your nose is bleeding.

98
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,250
- Oh, God!     - You're bleeding.

99
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,620
Ah. Ah, not again.

100
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:03,750
This happened when my grandfather died.

101
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:05,920
It's... Ugh, sorry.

102
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:07,800
Oh, gross, unh.

103
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:11,720
Okay. So I'm sorry. What did you wanna tell me?

104
00:07:15,050 --> 00:07:16,510
- Um...     - Ugh.

105
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:21,020
Sorry. Sorry.

106
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,890
Okay.

107
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:25,360
I, uh...

108
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:28,020
I can't see you anymore.

109
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:31,780
Yeah, I know, it's ridiculous. I can't see you, either.

110
00:07:33,910 --> 00:07:36,240
I think you'll find this room more to your liking.

111
00:07:36,410 --> 00:07:37,660
Okay, great.

112
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:43,750
They say he's only got half a tank left.

113
00:07:44,670 --> 00:07:48,380
Half a tank? We still got a lot of high-speed chasing to do!

114
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:51,630
- We're switching rooms again.     - What? Why?

115
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,590
This is a garden-view room and we paid for an ocean-view room.

116
00:07:55,800 --> 00:08:00,970
Our last ocean-view room was unacceptable to you.

117
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:04,980
Excuse me. Um, can I talk to you over here for just a second?

118
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:06,650
Uh-huh.

119
00:08:09,730 --> 00:08:11,860
- Chandler.     - Yeah?

120
00:08:12,030 --> 00:08:15,740
Look, these clowns are trying to take us for a ride. I won't let them.

121
00:08:15,910 --> 00:08:17,870
We're not a couple of suckers.

122
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:20,240
I hear you, Mugsy.

123
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,750
But, look, all these rooms are fine.

124
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:26,540
Okay? Can you just pick one so I can watch the...

125
00:08:26,710 --> 00:08:30,500
Have a perfect, magical weekend together with you?

126
00:08:34,550 --> 00:08:36,430
- Okay, this one I like.     - Nothing.

127
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:38,090
Nothing. It's over.

128
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:41,720
Damn it, this is regularly scheduled programming!

129
00:08:42,810 --> 00:08:44,640
Can we turn the TV off, okay?

130
00:08:44,810 --> 00:08:47,270
Do we really wanna spend the weekend like this?

131
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:50,690
I'm sorry, am I getting in the way of all the room-switching fun?

132
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:54,030
- Ha, ha, don't blame me for ruining tonight.     - Who should I blame?

133
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:56,860
The nice bellman who had to drag our luggage to 10 rooms?

134
00:08:57,030 --> 00:08:59,030
Or the idiot who thought he could drive...

135
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:02,540
...from Albany to Canada on a half a tank of gas?

136
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:05,960
Do not speak ill of the dead.

137
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:11,750
We're supposed to be spending a romantic weekend together.

138
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,170
What's the matter with you?

139
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:16,090
I just wanna watch a little television. What's the big deal?

140
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:17,970
Jeez, relax, Mom.

141
00:09:20,890 --> 00:09:22,140
What did you say?

142
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:26,100
I said, "Jeez, relax, Mon."

143
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,360
Hey.

144
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:43,700
Rachel, I've been wanting to tell you something and I just have to get it out.

145
00:09:43,870 --> 00:09:45,500
Okay. All right. What's up?

146
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:48,290
Okay.

147
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:54,340
You know how you told me I should do whatever it takes to fix my marriage?

148
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:57,720
Yeah, I told you to give Emily whatever she wants.

149
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:04,510
And while that was good advice, you should know that what she wants...

150
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:07,140
Yeah?

151
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:11,730
...is for me not to see you anymore.

152
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:18,740
Well, that's crazy. You can't do that. What are you gonna tell her?

153
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:26,330
Oh, my God.

154
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:29,370
Oh, you've already agreed to this, haven't you?

155
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,670
It's awful, I know. Uh, it's... Heh.

156
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:36,670
I mean, I feel terrible, but I have to do this if I want my marriage to work.

157
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:41,380
And I do. I have to make this marriage work. I have to.

158
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:49,230
But the good thing is, we can still see each other until she gets here.

159
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,150
Oh!

160
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:57,480
Oh, lucky me! Oh, my God! That is good news, Ross!

161
00:10:57,650 --> 00:11:01,150
I think that's the best news I've heard since LaPooh died!

162
00:11:03,990 --> 00:11:09,040
You have no idea what a nightmare this has been. Uh, this is so hard.

163
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,540
Oh, yeah, really? Is it, Ross?

164
00:11:11,710 --> 00:11:15,630
- Well, let me make this a little easier for you.     - What are you doing?

165
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,960
- Storming out.     - Rachel, this is your apartment.

166
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:20,970
Yeah? Well, that's how mad I am!

167
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:37,110
Damn Rolos!

168
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:39,780
- Hey, you're back.     - Hey.

169
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,280
How was your conference?

170
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:45,660
It was terrible. I fought with my colleagues for the entire time.

171
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:48,160
Are you kidding with this?

172
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:50,700
Uh, so your weekend was a bust?

173
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:54,290
Uh, no, I got to see Donald Trump waiting for an elevator.

174
00:11:56,130 --> 00:11:57,840
- Hi.     - Hey, you're back too.

175
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,010
Yeah. Um, Chandler, could I talk to you outside for a second?

176
00:12:01,170 --> 00:12:04,180
- How was your chef thing?     - Ugh. It was awful.

177
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:07,050
I guess some people don't appreciate really good food.

178
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:09,970
Maybe it was the kind of food that tasted good at first...

179
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:13,270
...but then made everybody vomit and have diarrhea.

180
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:18,230
- Chandler.     - Monica.

181
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,820
I wanna know how much the room was. I'll pay my half.

182
00:12:23,990 --> 00:12:25,110
Okay, fine. $300.

183
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:28,660
- Three hundred dollars?     - Yeah. Just think of it as $25 per room.

184
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:34,960
What are you guys woofing about?

185
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:37,130
Chandler stole a 20 from my purse!

186
00:12:37,630 --> 00:12:39,750
No!

187
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:44,420
You know what? Now that I think about it...

188
00:12:44,590 --> 00:12:47,800
...I constantly find myself without 20s, and you...

189
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:49,930
...always have lots.

190
00:12:55,230 --> 00:12:57,480
You should've seen the look on her face.

191
00:12:57,650 --> 00:13:01,230
I don't want Rachel to hate me. I don't know what to do.

192
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,570
- You want my advice?     - Yes. Please.

193
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:06,700
- You're not gonna like it.     - That's okay.

194
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,780
You got married too fast.

195
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:13,540
- That's not advice.     - I told you.

196
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,920
I'm going to the bathroom.

197
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:24,670
Man, if anyone asked me to give up any of you, I don't think I could do it.

198
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:25,880
Me neither.

199
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:27,840
Maybe I could do it.

200
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:33,350
- Hi.     - Hey.

201
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:36,350
I know you guys heard about the whole thing with me and Ross.

202
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:41,020
But I've been obsessing about it all day and would love not to talk about it.

203
00:13:41,190 --> 00:13:43,400
Uh, I don't know if this falls under that category...

204
00:13:43,570 --> 00:13:46,650
...but, uh, Ross is right back there.

205
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:49,450
- That's not Ross.     - Oh, no, not that guy.

206
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,570
He does look like him, though.

207
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,910
Okay. Ross is in the bathroom.

208
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:59,120
Oh, my God. It's happening. It's already started. I'm Kip.

209
00:13:59,290 --> 00:14:01,540
- What?     - Yeah, you're not Kip.

210
00:14:01,710 --> 00:14:03,210
Do you even know who Kip is?

211
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,380
Who cares? You're Rachel.

212
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:11,260
Who's Kip?

213
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:14,060
Kip, my old roommate. We all hung out together.

214
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:16,770
- Oh, that poor bastard.     - Mm-hm.

215
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:20,520
See? You told me the story. He and Monica dated.

216
00:14:20,690 --> 00:14:22,940
They broke up, they couldn't be in the same room.

217
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:24,940
You all promised you'd stay his friend.

218
00:14:25,110 --> 00:14:27,780
And what happened? He got phased out.

219
00:14:27,950 --> 00:14:30,660
- You're not gonna be phased out.     - Well, of course I am.

220
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:34,700
It won't happen to Ross. He's your brother, your old college roommate.

221
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:37,910
It was a matter of time before someone had to leave the group.

222
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,870
I always assumed Phoebe would be the one to go.

223
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:45,460
Honey, come on, you live far away, you're not related.

224
00:14:45,630 --> 00:14:47,130
You lift right out.

225
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:54,930
Hey.

226
00:14:55,260 --> 00:14:57,180
Hey, Mr. Bing.

227
00:14:57,350 --> 00:15:00,770
That, uh, hotel you stayed at called.

228
00:15:01,310 --> 00:15:04,230
Said someone left an eyelash curler in your room.

229
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,820
Yes, that was mine.

230
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:13,110
I figured you hooked up with some girl and she left it.

231
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:15,990
Yes, that would have made more sense.

232
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:20,040
You know, I don't even feel like I know you anymore, man.

233
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:24,830
All right, uh, look, I'm just gonna ask you this one time, all right?

234
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,590
And whatever you say, I'll believe you.

235
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:31,470
Were you or were you not on a gay cruise...

236
00:15:31,630 --> 00:15:33,090
...on a gay cruise?

237
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,440
Phoebe.

238
00:15:52,110 --> 00:15:55,070
I'm sorry about the whole lifting-out thing.

239
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:59,040
You gotta come with me.

240
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,830
- Come where?     - Wherever I go.

241
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,420
Come on, you and me, we'll start a new group. We're the best ones.

242
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:11,590
Okay, but try to get Joey too.

243
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:17,760
Pheebs, do you mind if I speak to Rachel alone for a sec?

244
00:16:17,930 --> 00:16:20,010
Oh, sure, yeah.

245
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:23,390
Bye, Ross.

246
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,770
Forever.

247
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,230
- Ahem.     - Hi.

248
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:31,480
Hi.

249
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:34,610
What are you doing here? Isn't this against the rules?

250
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,450
I talked to Monica.

251
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:43,790
Look, I'm the one who made the choice.

252
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:46,790
I'm the one who's making things change.

253
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:50,340
So I should be the one to, you know, step back.

254
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:53,590
- Oh, Ross...     - No, no, it's okay. Really.

255
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,550
Plenty of people just see their sisters at Thanksgiving...

256
00:16:56,720 --> 00:17:00,600
...and just see their college roommates at reunions...

257
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,850
...and just see Joey at Burger King.

258
00:17:08,650 --> 00:17:09,900
So is that better?

259
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:15,990
No, it's not better.

260
00:17:16,740 --> 00:17:19,030
I still don't get to see you.

261
00:17:21,450 --> 00:17:25,290
Well, what would you do, Rach? If you were me, what would you do?

262
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:33,380
Well...

263
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:37,130
...for starters, I would have said the right name at my wedding.

264
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:46,140
I can't believe this is happening.

265
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,610
I know.

266
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:54,900
I am so sorry.

267
00:17:56,570 --> 00:17:58,320
I know that too.

268
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,410
Ahem. Hey, Rach?

269
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:12,040
Sorry to interrupt, but, uh, Phoebe said you wanted to talk to me about a trip.

270
00:18:17,550 --> 00:18:20,720
- Hey.     - Hi.

271
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,600
I just came over to drop off...

272
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,520
...nothing.

273
00:18:29,230 --> 00:18:31,100
So that weekend kind of sucked, huh?

274
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:33,110
Yeah, it did.

275
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:35,900
So I guess this is over?

276
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:39,860
- What?     - Well, you know, you and me.

277
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:41,740
I mean, it had to end sometime.

278
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:44,240
Why exactly?

279
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:46,830
Because of the weekend. We had a fight.

280
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,500
Chandler, that's crazy.

281
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:53,080
Ha, ha. If you give up every time you have a fight with someone...

282
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:56,050
...you'd never be with anyone longer than...

283
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:59,510
Oh.

284
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:04,510
So this isn't over?

285
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,560
You are so cute!

286
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:13,650
No, no. It was a fight.

287
00:19:13,810 --> 00:19:18,150
You deal with it and you move on. It's nothing to freak out about.

288
00:19:18,860 --> 00:19:21,820
- Really? Okay, great.      - Heh.

289
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:24,990
Aw. Welcome to an adult relationship.

290
00:19:28,910 --> 00:19:30,250
We're in a relationship?

291
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:36,500
- I'm afraid so.     - Okay.

292
00:19:42,010 --> 00:19:43,590
- Hey.     - Hey.

293
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:47,140
Oh, hey, Monica, I heard you saw Donald Trump at your convention.

294
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:49,390
Yeah, saw him waiting for an elevator.

295
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:55,230
Rach, can I borrow your eyelash curler? I lost mine.

296
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,360
Yeah, it's in the bathroom.

297
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,950
Oh! Oh!

298
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,120
- Joey, can I talk to you for a second?     - Ooh, oh!

299
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:08,870
- Joey, I need to talk to you.     - Oh! Oh!

300
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:11,000
Oh, oh, oh!

301
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:23,220
Yes.

302
00:20:24,010 --> 00:20:27,180
You? And you?

303
00:20:27,890 --> 00:20:30,350
Yes, but you cannot tell anyone. No one knows.

304
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:32,350
But how? When?

305
00:20:32,850 --> 00:20:35,230
- It happened in London.      - In London!

306
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:41,690
The reason we didn't tell anyone was we didn't wanna make a big deal out of it.

307
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:45,570
But it is a big deal! I have to tell someone!

308
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:48,280
No, no, no. You can't.

309
00:20:48,490 --> 00:20:51,620
Please, please. We just don't wanna deal with telling everyone.

310
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:54,120
Please, just promise you won't tell.

311
00:20:57,710 --> 00:20:59,840
All right.

312
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,340
Man, this is unbelievable!

313
00:21:03,510 --> 00:21:06,510
I mean, it's great! But...

314
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:10,050
I know. It's great! Ha, ha.

315
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:12,930
Oh, I don't wanna see that!

316
00:21:15,690 --> 00:21:18,100
We're so stupid.

317
00:21:18,310 --> 00:21:21,690
Do you know what's going on in there? They're trying to take Joey.

318
00:21:28,070 --> 00:21:32,330
"The most popular Phoebe in tennis is called the overhand Phoebe. Heh.

319
00:21:32,490 --> 00:21:35,870
If you win, you must slap your opponent on the Phoebe and say, 'Hi, Phoebe!"'

320
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:40,880
Oh, that's cute. We really all enjoyed it.

321
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:43,130
- But you know it doesn't count.      - For what?

322
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:47,340
Just count in our heads as good Mad Libs.

323
00:21:48,010 --> 00:21:50,340
- I guess fun time's over.     - Yeah, I'm done.

324
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:52,970
Wait, guys, if we follow the rules...

325
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:55,520
...it's still fun and it means something.

326
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,020
I'm gonna take off.

327
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:59,440
Guys, rules are good!

328
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:01,400
Rules help control the fun.

329
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:04,320
Oh!

